==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{af|la||alt1=*bitu|-men}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*gʷétu|t=resin, gum}}, borrowed from an {{bor|la|itc-sbl}} language, traditionally assumed to be a {{bor|la|cel|nocat=1}} one (compare {{m+|la|betulla}}), where the shift of *''gʷ'' to ''b'' is regular.<ref>{{R:cel:Matasovic 2009|pages=64–65|head=*betu-}}</ref> The raising of the first vowel might come from the Osco-Umbrian variety, or have been developed in Latin, as occasionally happens after labials; compare {{m|la|firmus}}, {{m|la|vitulus}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|bitūmen, -minis|pages=72–73}}</ref> Cognate with {{cog|gd|bìth|t=resin, gum}}, {{cog|en|cud}}, {{cog|sa|जतु|t=lac, gum}}.

